From: TicWatch Nerves maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: rover: describe fixed SDIO I/O voltage

Rubyfish's stock overlay shares rover-wlan.dtsi: SDIO I/O is 1.8 V,
with 4 mA active pin drive. Without vqmmc, sdhci-msm does not configure
the pad voltage capabilities correctly; enumeration times out as soon
as the clock changes from 400 kHz to 50 MHz. A fixed 1.8 V declaration
restores enumeration. This describes the existing rail and does not
operate an unverified external regulator GPIO. Keep the supported 50 MHz.

Match the pin settings used in the successful RAM test. The 4 mA setting
alone was not a fix for the separate WPA authentication-offload issue.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm429w-mobvoi-rover.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm429w-mobvoi-rover.dts
@@ -91,3 +91,11 @@
+	wifi_vqmmc: wifi-vqmmc-regulator {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "wifi-vqmmc";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+		regulator-always-on;
+	};
+
 	sdio_pwrseq: sdio-pwrseq {
 		compatible = "mmc-pwrseq-simple";
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
@@ -360,3 +368,4 @@
 &sdhc_2 {
+	vqmmc-supply = <&wifi_vqmmc>;
 	cap-sd-highspeed;
 	cap-sdio-irq;
@@ -385,3 +394,15 @@
+&sdc2_default {
+	clk-pins {
+		drive-strength = <4>;
+	};
+	cmd-pins {
+		drive-strength = <4>;
+	};
+	data-pins {
+		drive-strength = <4>;
+	};
+};
+
 &sleep_clk {
 	clock-frequency = <32768>;
 };
